 :context
 "ISIC Rev.5 1394 (Manufacture of cordage, rope, twine and netting) had
  no prior actor implementation -- gh api confirmed both
  repos/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C1394 and
  repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1394 returned 404 before this
  work started. The registry's live {:id \"1394\" :name \"Manufacture
  of cordage, rope, twine and netting\" :maturity :spec ...} entry was
  verified against a fresh clone (via the GitHub git-data blob API, not
  the CDN-cached raw.githubusercontent.com mirror) before any work
  began, confirming no ID/name mismatch. Fresh, from-scratch scaffold,
  built as part of a smaller, carefully verified batch (capable model +
  mandatory verification) after an earlier 18-agent haiku batch's 61%
  defect rate; 120+ consecutive agents on this stricter protocol had
  succeeded prior to this one. Module shape mirrors sibling
  cloud-itonami-isic-1391 (Manufacture of knitted and crocheted
  fabrics)'s verified module shape -- the most recently created
  :implemented 13xx textile-family actor at the time of this work, and
  the first to use the corrected io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph +
  io.github.kotoba-lang/langchain :local/root dependency convention
  (com-junkawasaki/langgraph-clj is now confirmed a GitHub
  rename-redirect to kotoba-lang/langgraph) -- domain-adapted for
  cordage/rope/twine/netting manufacturing (fibre-twisting machines,
  braiding machines, winding lines), substituting length-meters for
  volume-yards and adding an eleventh governor check for
  breaking-strength-kn (breaking-strength-test plausibility), the
  task's own explicit domain requirement."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Coordination-only actor. Closed four-op allowlist, all :effect
   :propose: log-production-batch, schedule-maintenance,
   flag-safety-concern (always escalates), coordinate-shipment. An op
   outside this set is a HARD hold (unknown-op-violations)."
  :governor-rules
  "Eleven HARD, permanent, un-overridable checks elaborating four
   blueprint invariants: (1) plant/batch record must be independently
   verified/registered before any action -- equipment-not-verified
   (schedule-maintenance) / batch-not-verified (coordinate-shipment) /
   shipment-volume-exceeded (independently recomputed against the
   batch's own logged length-meters, never the proposal's own claim);
   (2) request :effect must be :propose only (not-propose-effect,
   evaluated first, unconditional); (3) any proposal touching
   twisting/braiding-line-equipment control is a hard, permanent block
   -- equipment-control-blocked (closed proposal-:effect allowlist) AND
   line-operate-blocked (:direct-operate? true on a maintenance
   proposal), two independent layers, neither ever a member of any
   phase's :auto set; (4) closed op-allowlist (unknown-op). Plus
   already-scheduled (double-schedule guard), invalid-grade,
   invalid-breaking-strength (this build's own domain-specific
   addition -- must be a strictly positive, physically plausible
   kilonewton reading, > 0 and <= 20000.0), invalid-defect-rate. Soft
   confidence/high-stakes gate: flag-safety-concern always escalates
   regardless of confidence (high-stakes set + cordageops.phase's
   permanent absence of this op from every phase's :auto set -- two
   independent layers agree); low confidence (<0.6) also escalates.
   Only log-production-batch may auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when
   governor-clean."
  :module-shape
  "cordageops.store (MemStore, batches + equipment directories seeded
   with a verified/registered batch with shipping headroom, a
   verified/registered batch nearly fully shipped, and an UNVERIFIED
   batch; one verified/registered twisting-machine unit and one
   UNVERIFIED braiding-machine unit), advisor (CordageAdvisor, mock +
   real-LLM seam via langchain.model), governor (Cordage & Netting
   Plant Operations Governor), phase (0->3 rollout), operation
   (langgraph-clj StateGraph via langgraph.graph, interrupt-before
   #{:request-approval}), sim (demo driver exercising all three
   happy-path escalate/approve flows plus all eleven HARD-hold
   scenarios directly)."}
